; What yacc's tables and lexer feedback settle for the standard's grammar, written out for a
; parser that takes the first alternative that matches (hbnf's `|`): where one alternative is the
; front of another the longer is written first, and a reserved word is not a command name.
; These rules replace the standard's own of the same names.

ws = SP | HTAB | BS LF | "#" *~LF

; the inside of $( ... ): a program, then the closing parenthesis (a rule of its own, so
; white space before it is skipped)
cmdsub-body = program cmdsub-close
cmdsub-close = ")"

; Rule 1 (and 7a): a reserved word is not a command name.  (`in` is reserved only after
; `for name` and `case word`, so it is not on this list.)
cmd_name = WORD - reserved
reserved = If | Then | Else | Elif | Fi | Do | Done | Case | Esac | While | Until | For | Lbrace | Rbrace | Bang

; ---- ordered choice takes the first alternative that matches, and an alternative that is the front of
; another reads the same text again when it is not taken: with commands inside words ($( ), back-quotes)
; and compound commands inside compound commands that is exponential.  So each choice between a
; shorter and a longer form is written as the shorter with an optional rest ("x [ y ]", which is
; "x y | x" without reading x twice), in the order the standard's alternatives give the same
; language.  The tree has an optional field where the standard has two alternatives. ----
program          = linebreak [ complete_commands linebreak ]
complete_command = list [ separator_op ]
command          = function_definition
                 | compound_command [ redirect_list ]
                 | simple_command
function_body    = compound_command [ redirect_list ]
compound_list    = linebreak term [ separator ]
if_clause        = If compound_list Then compound_list [ else_part ] Fi
else_part        = Elif compound_list Then compound_list [ else_part ]
                 | Else compound_list
case_clause      = Case WORD linebreak In linebreak [ case_list ] [ case_item_ns ] Esac
case_item        = [ '(' ] pattern ')' case_body DSEMI linebreak
case_item_ns     = [ '(' ] pattern ')' case_body
case_body        = compound_list
                 | linebreak
simple_command   = cmd_prefix [ cmd_rest ]
                 | cmd_name [ cmd_suffix ]
cmd_rest         = cmd_word [ cmd_suffix ]
pipeline         = Bang pipe_sequence
                 | pipe_sequence

; `;;` and `&&` are tokens of their own (DSEMI, AND_IF); a lone `;` or `&` is the separator
separator_op     = AMP
                 | SEMI
sequential_sep   = SEMI linebreak
                 | newline_list
